= The 60-Second Self-Test

Cover the answers, say each one aloud, then check. If any answer takes longer than ten seconds, revisit that section.

- *When were the first general elections held and what was their scale?* → October 1951 - February 1952; 17 crore+ voters, 489 Lok Sabha + about 3,200 MLAs.
- *Why were symbols printed on ballots?* → About 85% of voters could not read — pictures made universal franchise workable.
- *Congress seats in 1952 / 1957 / 1962?* → 364 of 489; 371 of 494; 361 of 494.
- *Which party was the largest opposition in all three elections?* → CPI (16, 27, 29 seats).
- *What happened in Kerala in 1957 and 1959?* → 1957: CPI under EMS Namboodiripad formed the world's first elected communist government; 1959: the Centre dismissed it and imposed President's rule.
- *Who founded the Swatantra Party, when, and with what idea?* → C. Rajagopalachari, 1959 — free enterprise against the licence raj.
- *Name the four major opposition parties with one founder each.* → Socialists (JP Narayan/Lohia), CPI (1925), Jana Sangh (S.P. Mookerjee, 1951), Swatantra (Rajaji, 1959).
- *State the Congress system in one line.* → One dominant party of consensus + opposition parties working as pressure + real competition inside factions.
- *Why was the Congress called a coalition?* → It housed many ideologies, castes and classes as factions — groups fought for power INSIDE the umbrella instead of leaving it.
- *Which states escaped Congress sweeps in this era?* → Kerala (CPI), J&K (National Conference), Punjab-PEPSU (Akali Dal), Madras (DMK rising), West Bengal and Orissa pockets (left).

