= Detailed Solutions

Each solution shows the reasoning, not just the verdict — cover the answer line, attempt the question, then compare.

#solution(1, [Polling ran in phases from October 1951 to February 1952 — the first election on universal adult franchise. 1950 saw the Election Commission's creation, not the polling.], answer: [B])

#solution(2, [Sukumar Sen administered the giant 1951-52 exercise, including the symbol system for illiterate voters. T.N. Seshan is a later Chief Election Commissioner (1990s) — a deliberate distractor.], answer: [A])

#solution(3, [CPI won 16 seats in 1952 — the largest opposition. The Socialists contested as two separate parties (SP 12 + KMPP 9) and merged into the PSP only after the election; Swatantra did not exist until 1959, and Jana Sangh won only 3.], answer: [C])

#solution(4, [Kerala 1957: E.M.S. Namboodiripad headed the first government anywhere elected on a communist programme. West Bengal's Left Front governments came only in 1977 — a time-gap distractor.], answer: [C])

#solution(5, [C. Rajagopalachari (Rajaji) — former Governor-General — founded Swatantra in 1959 with N.G. Ranga and K.M. Munshi, on free enterprise against the licence raj.], answer: [D])

#solution(6, [The Jana Sangh (1951, Syama Prasad Mookerjee) built its politics on cultural unity — one country, one nation, one culture — with Kashmir integration, Hindi and a uniform civil code as signature demands.], answer: [C])

#solution(7, [Under first-past-the-post, whoever leads a constituency takes the whole seat. Congress led widely but modestly almost everywhere, so 45% of votes compounded into 74% of seats. The elections were free — option C is the classic wrong reflex.], answer: [B])

#solution(8, [Political scientist Rajni Kothari named the pattern the Congress system: a party of dominance plus parties of pressure, with real competition inside Congress factions. Granville Austin wrote on the Constitution — a deliberate distractor.], answer: [A])

#solution(9, [In 1959 the Centre, on the Governor's report over the liberation-struggle protests, imposed President's rule — the first dismissal of an elected state government. No no-confidence motion or court ruling was involved.], answer: [D])

#solution(10, [The Socialist Party (JP Narayan, Lohia) merged with Kripalani's Kisan Mazdoor Praja Party in 1952 to form the Praja Socialist Party. The Janata Party belongs to 1977 — a different era.], answer: [B])

